{"text": "Our team has reviewed the incident report submitted last week regarding the intermittent outages in the European region. The root cause appears to be a misconfigured load balancer that drops connections when traffic spikes above a threshold during the evening peak. We have applied a temporary fix, but customers may still notice slow responses until the permanent change is deployed next Tuesday. Our team has reviewed the incident report submitted last week regarding the intermittent outages in the European region. The root cause appears to be a misconfigured load balancer that drops connections when traffic spikes above a threshold during the evening peak. We have applied a temporary fix, but customers may still notice slow responses until the permanent change is deployed next Tuesday. Our team has reviewed the incident report submitted last week regarding the intermittent outages in the European region. The root cause appears to be a misconfigured load balancer that drops connections when traffic spikes above a threshold during the evening peak. We have applied a temporary fix, but customers may still notice slow responses until the permanent change is deployed next Tuesday. Our team has reviewed the incident report submitted last week regarding the intermittent outages in the European region. The root cause appears to be a misconfigured load balancer that drops connections when traffic spikes above a threshold during the evening peak. We have applied a temporary fix, but customers may still notice slow responses until the permanent change is deployed next Tuesday. Please confirm whether this explanation is enough for your compliance review.", "ids": [2, 7711, 2434, 815, 20301, 506, 10530, 2072, 13450, 1774, 2069, 8859, 506, 70127, 101990, 528, 506, 6693, 4128, 236761, 669, 5989, 4400, 7412, 531, 577, 496, 3930, 126240, 3711, 150731, 600, 17221, 13792, 1056, 8827, 57952, 2787, 496, 14272, 1913, 506, 9137, 11519, 236761, 1191, 735, 6055, 496, 15404, 7562, 2